ting-map naturality.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-punctured-rn-deformation-retracts-onto-the-sphere","used_for":"Punctured Euclidean-space homology example.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-right-derived-functors-from-two-supplied-injective-resolution-data-are-naturally-isomorphic","used_for":"Transport and comparison of right-derived data.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-right-derived-functors-relative-to-supplied-data-are-additive-functors","used_for":"Right-derived delta-functor structure.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-the-category-of-abelian-groups-is-monoidal-under-the-tensor-product","used_for":"Ab-enrichment equivalence.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-the-category-of-small-categories-is-cartesian-closed","used_for":"Cat-enrichment identification.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-the-hom-bifunctor-of-a-preadditive-category-takes-values-in-abelian-groups","used_for":"Ab-enrichment equivalence.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-the-internal-hom-composition-morphism","used_for":"Self-enrichment of a right-closed base.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-the-unit-is-an-internal-hom-unit","used_for":"Global elements, representables, and enriched Yoneda.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-zero-th-left-derived-functor-of-a-right-exact-functor-recovers-the-functor","used_for":"Degree-zero left-derived identification.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-zero-th-right-derived-functor-of-a-left-exact-functor-recovers-the-functor","used_for":"Degree-zero right-derived identification.","opened":true}],"concerns":[{"id":"def-enriched-category","concern":"The displayed left and right unit laws use the wrong composition indices. After $j_B\\otimes1$, the composite has source $\\mathcal A(B,B)\\otimes\\mathcal A(A,B)$ and requires $M_{A,B,B}$, not $M_{A,A,B}$; after $1\\otimes j_A$, it requires $M_{A,A,B}$, not $M_{A,B,B}$. Both displayed composites are ill-typed.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"thm-left-derived-functors-form-a-homological-delta-functor","concern":"The statement calls $(L_n^PF):\\mathcal D\\to\\mathcal B$ a homological delta functor “on $\\mathcal D$”, but $\\mathcal D$ is assumed only to be a class of objects. The governing definition requires an abelian source category and quantifies over all its short exact sequences; no full abelian/exact-subcategory or closure hypothesis on $\\mathcal D$ is supplied.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"thm-right-derived-functors-form-a-cohomological-delta-functor","concern":"The same domain defect occurs here: $\\mathcal D$ is only a class of objects, yet the conclusion asserts a cohomological delta functor on it. No category structure or closure under the relevant short exact sequences is assumed.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"thm-derived-functors-are-universal-delta-functors","concern":"Its use of the two positive-degree effaceability propositions omits their extra domain hypotheses: each requires every object of the datum's class $\\mathcal D$ to admit the relevant projective epimorphism or injective monomorphism with the projective/injective object still in $\\mathcal D$. Enough projectives or injectives in the ambient source category alone does not provide that.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"fs-a-degree-zero-natural-transformation-between-delta-functors-always-extends","concern":"The proposed target $T_0=H_0$, $T_n=0$ for $n>0$, with zero connecting maps is generally not a homological delta functor: its required long sequence would contain $0\\to H_0(A)\\to H_0(B)$, but the cited nonzero connecting morphism $H_1(C)\\to H_0(A)$ makes this map nonmonic. Thus it cannot witness a degree-zero transformation between delta functors.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"cex-equal-homology-does-not-imply-homotopy-equivalence","concern":"Step 1.3 concludes that $\\pi_1(X)$ is not isomorphic to $\\pi_1(Y)$ by contrasting $\\mathbb Z^2$ with $F_2$, but the proof establishes $\\pi_1(Y)\\cong F_2$ only later in step 2.1. Reordering the conclusion after step 2.1 closes the gap.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"}],"alerts":[],"seams_checked":[]}